== D.1 Complete Solutions

#sol-item(1, "A")[
  Vertically opposite angles are equal, so the required angle is $88^degree$. The angle adjacent to it would be $92^degree$. *Chapter 1.*
]

#sol-item(2, "B")[
  The exterior angle equals the sum of the two interior opposite angles: $66 + 54 = 120^degree$. *Chapter 2.*
]

#sol-item(3, "D")[
  Opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral are supplementary: $180 - 121 = 59^degree$. *Chapter 3.*
]

#sol-item(4, "C")[
  The radii differ by $3$ cm and sum to $9$ cm; since the centres are $3$ cm apart the circles touch internally, so they have $1$ common tangents. *Chapter 4.*
]

#sol-item(5, "B")[
  $A = 1/2 d_1 d_2 = 1/2 times 8 times 8 = 32$ cm². *Chapter 5.*
]

#sol-item(6, "D")[
  $V = l b h = 5 times 9 times 9 = 405$ cm³. *Chapter 6.*
]

#sol-item(7, "C")[
  Latitude difference $= 10^degree$, so the distance is $10 times 111 = 1110$ km. *Chapter 7.*
]

#sol-item(8, "A")[
  $y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)$: $y - 0 = -3(x - -2)$, giving $y = -3x - 6$. *Chapter 8.*
]

#sol-item(9, "D")[
  $cos theta = frac(12, 13)$ from the definitions SOH CAH TOA. *Chapter 9.*
]

#sol-item(10, "C")[
  The back bearing is the forward bearing $plus.minus 180^degree$: $"035"^degree$ $plus.minus 180^degree = 215^degree$. *Chapter 10.*
]

#sol-item(11, "A")[
  Angles on a straight line add to $180^degree$: $180 - 31 - 61 = 88^degree$. *Chapter 1.*
]

#sol-item(12, "B")[
  The base angles are equal and total $180 - 32 = 148^degree$, so each is $74^degree$. *Chapter 2.*
]

#sol-item(13, "D")[
  Angles in the same segment are equal. *Chapter 3.*
]

#sol-item(14, "B")[
  Two circles of radii $4$ and $5$ with centres $7$ apart: the number of intersections is $2$ (compare $7$ with $9$ and $1$). *Chapter 4.*
]

#sol-item(15, "A")[
  $A = 1/2 (a + b) h = 1/2 (13 + 4) times 4 = 34$ cm². *Chapter 5.*
]

#sol-item(16, "C")[
  $V = pi r^2 h = 22/7 times 49 times 19 = 2926$ cm³. *Chapter 6.*
]

#sol-item(17, "B")[
  On the equator the radius is $R$, and $1^degree = 110$ km, so the distance is $10 times 110 = 1100$ km. *Chapter 7.*
]

#sol-item(18, "D")[
  $y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)$: $y - 7 = -2(x - -1)$, giving $y = -2x + 5$. *Chapter 8.*
]

#sol-item(19, "C")[
  $tan theta = frac(3, 4)$ from the definitions SOH CAH TOA. *Chapter 9.*
]

#sol-item(20, "A")[
  Bearings are measured clockwise from North, so N60W is $"300"^degree$. *Chapter 10.*
]

#sol-item(21, "A")[
  Co-interior (allied) angles are supplementary: $180 - 53 = 127^degree$. *Chapter 1.*
]

#sol-item(22, "B")[
  $A = 1/2 b h = 1/2 times 10 times 19 = 95$ cm². *Chapter 2.*
]

#sol-item(23, "C")[
  The angle between the tangents and the angle at the centre are supplementary: $180 - 118 = 62^degree$. *Chapter 3.*
]

#sol-item(24, "D")[
  Two circles of radii $8$ and $2$ with centres $10$ apart: the number of intersections is $1$ (compare $10$ with $10$ and $6$). *Chapter 4.*
]

#sol-item(25, "B")[
  $A = 1/2 (a + b) h = 1/2 (4 + 5) times 6 = 27$ cm². *Chapter 5.*
]

#sol-item(26, "D")[
  $V = l b h = 4 times 3 times 9 = 108$ cm³. *Chapter 6.*
]

#sol-item(27, "A")[
  $15^degree$ of longitude is one hour, so $60^degree = 60/15 = 4$ hours. *Chapter 7.*
]

#sol-item(28, "C")[
  $d = sqrt(7^2 + 24^2) = sqrt(625) = 25$. *Chapter 8.*
]

#sol-item(29, "B")[
  $cos theta = frac(4, 5)$ from the definitions SOH CAH TOA. *Chapter 9.*
]

#sol-item(30, "A")[
  $"320"^degree$ $+ 90^degree = 50^degree$, so the new bearing is $"050"^degree$. *Chapter 10.*
]

